from pathlib import Path
import json,html,collections
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;s=json.loads((R/'SUMMARY.json').read_text());g=json.loads((R/'GROUPS.json').read_text())
rows=''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+html.escape(str(v))+'</td>' for v in [r['section'],r['reading'],r['lines'],r['pages'],r['slot_counts']['eligible'],r['V'],r['supported_pages'],'UNSUPPORTED'])+'</tr>' for r in s)
doc='''<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Manuscript support audit only</title><style>body{font:17px/1.55 system-ui;max-width:1100px;margin:40px auto;padding:20px;background:#f8faf7;color:#173c30}td,th{padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid #c4d4c9;text-align:left}table{border-collapse:collapse}</style><h1>All four panels unsupported under the frozen test</h1><p>No sh → qok outcome classification, association score or p-value was calculated. Only following-token readability was used for eligibility. H/F remain separate alternative readings, not independent replication.</p><table><tr><th>Section</th><th>Reading</th><th>Lines</th><th>Pages</th><th>Eligible fixed-position origins</th><th>V</th><th>Supported pages</th><th>Status</th></tr>'''+rows+'''</table>
<p>The threshold requires V≥80, at least8 supported pages and no page supplying more than25% of support. With V=0 the concentration fraction is undefined, not zero. Every unsupported page and selected group is retained.</p>
<h2>Handling verified</h2><p>Every saved line was reparsed from its raw transcription using the atlas cleaning policy and reconciled with atlas metadata and tokens. H/F panels use the same source loci, while keeping their different word boundaries and token counts. Source line lengths include unknown slots. Unknown origins and unknown immediate followers are excluded; no gaps or line ends are crossed.</p>
<p>Comma-adjacent uncertain tokens remain null; exclamation marks are removed as in the original atlas; brace comments become uncertainty barriers except the atlas's trailing-comment cleanup. Dedicated fixtures cover these cases. Positions are original zero-based indices, never ranks among readable or eligible tokens. This verifies consistency with the saved transcription policy, not the correctness of every manuscript reading.</p>
<h2>Critical scope limit</h2><p>The synthetic qualification used eight fixed origin positions: zero-based1,3,5,7,9,11,13,15. This audit retains those positions and does not search alternatives. Many manuscript lines do not reach the later positions, and many eligible origins fall outside them. Those exclusions are counted separately in SUMMARY.json.</p>
<p>Matching is within physical page and exact line length. The variable-length implementation partitions without pooling, but the earlier synthetic controls used fixed-length arrays. This audit is therefore a support check for the specified adaptation, not end-to-end validation of a manuscript test.</p>
<p>Hundreds of eligible origins do not imply movable comparisons: the chosen position pairs also require the same exact body in both positions, and discordant sh/ch rows in both orientations within a page/length group. No selected group supplies positive V. This demonstrates a limitation of this exact fixed-position method; it does not show that every legal rearrangement or other defensible test is unavailable.</p>
<p>The earlier bath association is neither rescored nor overturned. There is no new positive or negative association result. Any different position scheme, wider matching or pooling rule would be a new method requiring fresh qualification.</p>
<p><a href="PROTOCOL.json">Frozen audit rules</a> · <a href="SUMMARY.json">Panel coverage and exclusions</a> · <a href="LINE-AUDIT.json">Every line and slot</a> · <a href="GROUPS.json">Selected groups</a> · <a href="PAGES.json">Every page</a> · <a href="VERIFICATION.json">Verification</a> · <a href="FREEZE.json">Hashes</a></p>'''
(R/'report.html').write_text(doc,encoding='utf-8')
assert all((R/f).exists() for f in ['PROTOCOL.json','SUMMARY.json','LINE-AUDIT.json','GROUPS.json','PAGES.json','VERIFICATION.json','FREEZE.json'])
print('Selected groups by panel:',dict(collections.Counter(x['panel'] for x in g)));print('Positive V groups:',sum(x['V']>0 for x in g))
